.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt VPS-DEPLOY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vps-deploy
.Nd deploy approved pub5 services to the production VPS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm all | master | brgen | amber | bsdports | mrdamascy
.Nm
.Cm recover --plan
.Nm
.Cm recover --apply
.Ar run-id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the serialized production deploy entry point at
.Pa OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy .
Run it as
.Cm root
or as
.Cm dev
with passwordless
.Xr doas 1 .
When started as
.Cm dev ,
the script re-executes as root through
.Xr doas 1 .
Git fetch and checkout always run as
.Cm dev
so the production tree and GitHub credentials stay correctly owned.
Service lifecycle operations use
.Xr rcctl 8 .
Rails synchronization and tasks run through fixed helpers after dropping to the
owning application account.
.Pp
The command validates its target, checks bounded timing and capacity settings,
obtains the deploy lock, and runs the configured preflight, synchronization, CI,
restart, health and deploy-stamp steps. The exact order and restore behavior are
implemented in the script and the production runbook.
.Pp
Every top-level run has an atomic record under
.Pa /var/db/pub5/deploy_runs .
Records are owned by root:wheel, mode 0640, in a root:wheel 0750 directory.
They retain the pinned and previous revisions, original running-service
snapshot, ports, restore order, owner process identity and latest stage.
The directory is readable to the operator group so status and recovery tools
need no privileged command-dispatch service.
.Pp
Accepted targets are
.Cm all ,
.Cm master ,
.Cm brgen ,
.Cm amber ,
.Cm bsdports ,
and
.Cm mrdamascy .
Unknown targets are refused before deployment.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "VPS_DEPLOY_PREFLIGHT_SHA"
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_SHA
Commit to deploy. The default is fetched from
.Cm origin/main .
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_LOG_REF
A
.Cm local://deploys/<filename>.log
reference recorded in the recovery receipt. It is not opened on vm23; the
workstation collector owns the transcript file.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_PREFLIGHT_SHA
Commit whose boot was already proved by the operator's machine.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_CI_SHA
Commit whose
.Pa bin/ci
passed on the workstation. The host requires an exact SHA match and checks the
preinstalled production bundle in frozen, read-only mode. It does not install
gems or run the test suite.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_SKIP_PREFLIGHT
Break-glass preflight bypass. Setting this to
.Cm 1
also requires
.Ev I_UNDERSTAND_FAST_DEPLOY=1 .
.It Ev SKIP_CI
Setting this to
.Cm 1
is refused for Rails deployments. A matching workstation CI attestation is
required; vm23 never runs the Rails test suite.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_DRIFT
Setting this to
.Cm fail
refuses deployment when machine configuration differs from the repository.
.It Ev PUB4_DEPLOY_BROWSER_CHECKS
Setting this to
.Cm 1
adds browser checks after restart.
.El
.Ss Interrupted deployment recovery
.Cm recover --plan
lists records whose service restoration is pending. It is serialized by the
deploy lock, does not fetch or check out code, and does not start, stop or
restart services. A record is reported as live when its owner PID and process
fingerprint still match. It is ambiguous when a visible PID cannot be
identified, another deployer process may still be active, or the process-table
scan fails. A record is available only when its owner is gone or its PID was
reused, the service snapshot is complete, and no other deployer process is
visible.
.Pp
.Cm recover --apply
.Ar run-id
requires the exact ID shown by the plan. It refuses a live or ambiguous owner,
restores only services captured as running before that deploy, in the recorded
order, and verifies each service with
.Xr rcctl 8
plus each recorded app's loopback
.Pa /up
endpoint. Success marks the record recovered. Failed verification leaves it
pending for diagnosis and a later explicit retry.
.Pp
Recovery restores service availability only. It does not roll back the Git
checkout, database migrations or application data. It is never run automatically
at boot.
.Sh SECURITY
Do not bypass preflight during ordinary deployments. A successful
synchronization or TLS response alone does not establish that every application
is healthy. Inspect actual health and deployment records.
.Pp
Before live work, read
.Pa OPENBSD/RUNBOOK.md
and the owning tree README.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy --help
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy master
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy all
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy recover --plan
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy recover --apply 20261117T010000Z-all-12345
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr operator 1 ,
.Xr doas 1 ,
.Xr rcctl 8 ,
.Xr relayd 8
